  "body": "## Accepted result and published preprint\n\n**An explicit Frobenius corollary of established marginal entropy bounds for permanents**, Alec Kriebel. Published paper and verification package: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23430776 (https://zenodo.org/records/23430776).\n\nSelf-contained, credited corollary of Anari-Rezaei marginal entropy bounds, also implied by Anari (2026) and Dong-Jain (2026). For nonnegative row-stochastic A of order n>=1 and S=sum a_ij^2, per(A)<=exp(-n+e^4 S(1+log n)). Historical novelty and priority remain UNKNOWN. Extensive AI assistance; unrefereed; no external human peer review or formal proof-assistant certification.\n\n## Accepted scope and review\n\nFor every nonnegative row-stochastic n\u00d7n A, per(A)\u2264exp(-n+e^4\u03a3a_ij\u00b2 log(e/a_ij))\u2264exp(-n+e^4 S(1+log n)). Fixed S\u2264\u03b3 yields polynomial-times-e^-n; source van der Waerden lower bound completes the doubly stochastic target.\n\nNo original asymptotic-target gap asserted. Pure-power bound is excluded at n=1; an all-n prefactor is supplied. Priority remains unresolved; Anari\u2013Rezaei entropy inequality is credited, and scalar KL absorption/Frobenius consequence is the candidate contribution.\n\nThe result is accepted at the exact audited head `bdefe31b9d226c8f27008d13f57775d5de8df3d7`. 4 fresh independent complete AI whole-package reviews were completed, with the final review finding zero actionable issues. Subsequent bounded administrative adoption is recorded in the current external ROOT final seal; earlier status/counter/hold fields remain dated history. Prior mathematical results and proof dependencies are credited. Historical novelty and worldwide current openness are unestablished. AI tools were used extensively; this is an unrefereed preprint, without conventional human peer review or formal proof certification.\n\nThe repository Zenodo uploader verified the exact reviewed metadata and PDF/support bytes. The Google Workspace CLI recorded the DOI/details in the requested tracker with exact read-back. No GitHub release is created. Current audit and publication receipts: `audits/pr1064_30001073`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Preserved original PR description: dated submission history</summary>\n\n## Mathematical result\n\n**Complete accepted solution** of problem **30001073 / OWR-2090-026**, rank **1230**, on **Approach 1 of 5**. The independent analytic audit concludes PASS with no mathematical correction.\n\nFor every nonnegative row-stochastic n by n matrix A, with S=sum(a_ij\u00b2),\n\n    per(A) \u2264 exp(\u2212n + e\u2074 sum a_ij\u00b2 log(e/a_ij))\n           \u2264 exp(\u2212n + e\u2074 S(1+log n)).\n\nZero summands use their continuous value. If S\u2264\u03b3, then per(A)\u2264exp(e\u2074\u03b3)n^(e\u2074\u03b3)exp(\u2212n) for every n\u22651, and per(A)\u2264n^(3e\u2074\u03b3)exp(\u2212n) for n\u22652. The n=1 prefactor is necessary; a literal pure-power bound there is false. For the doubly stochastic source class, the already-known van der Waerden lower bound supplies the other direction. No stronger entrywise O(1/n) assumption is substituted.\n\nThe complete proof and substantive analytic audit retain the arbitrary-permutation entropy lemma, support and zero-entry treatment, Gibbs identity, total-mass KL bookkeeping, scalar absorption, Frobenius conversion, and block-diagonal example showing polynomial loss is necessary. The exponent is not claimed sharp.\n\n## Attribution and limits\n\nThe original question is Alexander Barvinok and Alex Samorodnitsky's problem 9 in [Oberwolfach Report 44/2008](https://doi.org/10.4171/owr/2008/44), printed pages 2549\u20132550. The direct Gibbs-marginal/random-order comparison is credited to [Anari\u2013Rezaei, arXiv:1811.02933v2](https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.02933v2), \u00a74, equation (6), page 12; [Radhakrishnan's classical entropy method](https://doi.org/10.1006/jcta.1996.2727) and the prior lower bound remain attributed.\n\nNo novelty, historical-priority or sharp-constant claim is made. The work is AI-assisted and unrefereed. Independent analytic audit is not external human peer review or proof-assistant certification. Bounded source checks do not certify absence of a prior consequence.\n\n## Edition boundary\n\nNine files are added under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/30001073/`. The proof's opening status sentence is updated; Sections 1\u20137 are otherwise retained byte-for-byte. All substantive mathematical audit reasoning and acceptance conditions are retained. Diagnostic sections/results and program references are removed without replacement computation prose. Report identities are explicitly rebound to the distributed edition. The public-source ledger retains eligible citations, PDF hashes/sizes and retrieval/inspection history. Edition preparation performed identity rechecks without new retrieval or scholarly inspection.\n\nNo source documents, source extracts/images, datasets, scripts, standalone computation outputs, logs, private coordination files or identities of nondistributed authored artifacts are included. This addition changes no queue entry or historical accounting and adds no proof-search turn.\n\n## Exact distributed identities\n\n- `ACCEPTANCE.md`: 1,935 bytes; SHA-256 `6ac9c9e3c558e47701c6fbed14f41c4c088c9b60ce7823269539597703348a8a`\n- `AUDIT.md`: 10,704 bytes; SHA-256 `71bb0d77c8eee077d0d4924601f1ba9f7fee26ebafa1e7ae1834406c74a8235b`\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,764 bytes; SHA-256 `5996d71763d828339937c0e089046167deb82eb8b2b135353771dd7994ac816a`\n- `PROOF.md`: 8,060 bytes; SHA-256 `fe83f40d5c6d96a526457eaae290e8b3f0a725b43a91286f818c4fb248db7205`\n- `PROVENANCE.md`: 4,371 bytes; SHA-256 `ccc4a5d328a58ae602b75be1a6c87f30b79f9aeb3bcd4901856ff31b83893cd1`\n- `README.md`: 2,183 bytes; SHA-256 `0648208519a60b7bb43d7fde1927180be31a169092994918f19b3b817a9f857e`\n- `SOURCE_LEDGER.md`: 4,637 bytes; SHA-256 `5331a444a3e0562b2bea3076ed96e4f2899034eb7a576f20d9c72cd7b051c211`\n- `STATUS.json`: 1,644 bytes; SHA-256 `162feba97faafb16aba1e5167b74e39e6a4a1cfbb7019c2fcb4fb2eb65cb6bb3`\n- `audit_manifest.json`: 1,386 bytes; SHA-256 `172dc6fd980b1da7b8e808bff50306f76889d40c6fcd5e534058f2fcd38747f1`\n\nThe manifest lists all nine members and hashes its other eight; this description independently pins the manifest.\n\n\n</details>\n",
